{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ND7YAs9MwYEdKrb8yraDBK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '核心 claim（phase-modulated compound severity exists and is robust）不变，但\n2\t  C11 从 ''scoring-independent eviction produces null gradient at all sparsities''\n3\t  降级为 ''scoring-independent eviction produces null-to-weak gradient, confirming attention-score\n4\t  mechanism is primary driver but not exclusive at extreme sparsity''。GPQA 跨 benchmark\n5\t  扩展确认 phase gradient 普适性，但 strategy specificity ratio 继续衰减（2-3×），强化 task-modulation\n6\t  叙事。Discussion 补充 boundary condition：extreme sparsity (s030) 下 任何 eviction 方法都可能触发弱\n7\t  phase-dependent effects。Rebuttal 核心策略：effect size comparison（importance d_z >> recency\n8\t  d_z 即使 s030 后者 nominally significant）。\n9\t\n10\t  '\n11\timagined_experiments:\n12\t- name: recency_s025\n13\t  plan_id: C11_recency_s025\n14\t  description: 'Recency-based eviction (scoring-independent control) at sparsity=0.25,\n15\t    n=100, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B. Tests whether phase gradient remains null\n16\t    at moderate-high sparsity.\n17\t\n18\t    '\n19\t  expected_results:\n20\t    n_problems: 100\n21\t    model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\n22\t    masking_method: recency\n23\t    sparsity: 0.25\n24\t    phase_gradient_median_diff: 0.032\n25\t    phase_gradient_median_diff_ci95:\n26\t    - -0.08\n27\t    - 0.16\n28\t    cohens_dz: 0.14\n29\t    p_value: 0.38\n30\t    significant: false\n31\t    low_phase_ii_median: 0.85\n32\t    high_phase_ii_median: 0.78\n33\t    low_high_ratio: 1.09\n34\t    comparison_importance_s025_dz: 0.95\n35\t    comparison_importance_s025_median_diff: 3.99\n36\t    importance_vs_recency_ratio: ~125×\n37\t    wilcoxon_p: 0.38\n38\t    bonferroni_p_k3: 1.0\n39\t  result_rationale: 'At s025, recency eviction removes the oldest 25% of KV entries\n40\t    regardless of attention scores. Since discrimination collapse is driven by importance-score\n41\t    judgment degradation after head pruning, recency eviction bypasses this mechanism\n42\t    entirely. The slight positive trend (d_z=0.14) reflects marginal information loss\n43\t    that differentially affects longer reasoning chains (low-sparsity phase has more\n44\t    accumulated context to lose), but the effect is far below significance. The key\n45\t    mechanistic argument holds: without attention-score-based selection, pruning doesn''t\n46\t    create the biased pseudo-random degradation pattern that amplifies compound severity\n47\t    in the low phase. At s025, total information loss from recency eviction is still\n48\t    below the critical threshold where any removal method would trigger phase effects.\n49\t\n50\t    '\n51\t  tables:\n52\t  - title: 'Table: Triple dissociation at s025'\n53\t    columns:\n54\t    - Strategy\n55\t    - median_diff\n56\t    - d_z\n57\t    - p\n58\t    - Significant\n59\t    rows:\n60\t    - - Importance\n61\t      - '3.99'\n62\t      - '0.95'\n63\t      - <1e-78\n64\t      - 'Yes'\n65\t    - - Random\n66\t      - '0.26'\n67\t      - '0.15'\n68\t      - 0.006 (Bonf.)\n69\t      - Marginal\n70\t    - - Recency\n71\t      - '0.03'\n72\t      - '0.14'\n73\t      - '0.38'\n74\t      - 'No'\n75\t  figures_description:\n76\t  - Bar chart showing phase gradient (median_diff) across three eviction strategies\n77\t    at s025. Importance bar dominates (~4.0), random barely visible (~0.26), recency\n78\t    near zero (~0.03). Error bars (95% CI) for recency cross zero.\n79\t  analysis: 's025 结果与 s015 (d_z=0.083) 方向一致：recency 在 moderate sparsity 范围内不产生 显著\n80\t    phase gradient。d_z 从 0.083 升至 0.14 表明存在微弱的 sparsity-dependent 趋势， 但仍远低于 importance\n81\t    的 d_z=0.95。Triple dissociation 在 s025 水平进一步确认： phase gradient 是 attention-score\n82\t    mechanism 的特有产物。Random 在 s025 的 marginal significance (n=500 数据 Bonf. p=0.006)\n83\t    与 recency NS 的对比值得注意——random masking 虽然不使用 importance scores，但其均匀采样仍受 head pruning\n84\t    后 score distribution 变化的间接影响；recency 完全脱离 score pathway，因此更 clean 作为 control。\n85\t\n86\t    '\n87\t- name: recency_s030\n88\t  plan_id: C11_recency_s030\n89\t  description: 'Recency-based eviction at sparsity=0.30 (extreme), n=100. Tests whether\n90\t    extreme information loss triggers weak phase-dependent effects even without score-based\n91\t    selection.\n92\t\n93\t    '\n94\t  expected_results:\n95\t    n_problems: 100\n96\t    model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\n97\t    masking_method: recency\n98\t    sparsity: 0.3\n99\t    phase_gradient_median_diff: 0.21\n100\t    phase_gradient_median_diff_ci95:\n101\t    - 0.02\n102\t    - 0.45\n103\t    cohens_dz: 0.32\n104\t    p_value: 0.028\n105\t    significant_uncorrected: true\n106\t    significant_bonferroni_k3: false\n107\t    bonferroni_p: 0.084\n108\t    low_phase_ii_median: 1.95\n109\t    high_phase_ii_median: 1.62\n110\t    low_high_ratio: 1.2\n111\t    comparison_importance_s030_dz: 1.13\n112\t    comparison_importance_s030_median_diff: 8.48\n113\t    importance_vs_recency_dz_ratio: 3.5×\n114\t    importance_vs_recency_mediandiff_ratio: ~40×\n115\t    wilcoxon_p: 0.028\n116\t  result_rationale: 'At extreme sparsity (s030), 30% of attention heads are pruned\n117\t    AND the oldest 30% of KV cache is evicted. Even though recency eviction doesn''t\n118\t    use attention scores, the sheer volume of information loss reaches a critical\n119\t    threshold where phase-dependent effects emerge through a different mechanism:\n120\t    low-sparsity phase (reasoning-heavy) relies more heavily on accumulated context\n121\t    from earlier tokens, and recency eviction disproportionately removes this early\n122\t    context. The effect is genuine but weak (d_z=0.32 vs importance d_z=1.13) and\n123\t    fails Bonferroni correction (k=3 strategies tested at s030). This establishes\n124\t    the boundary condition: at extreme sparsity, phase-dependent severity is not exclusively\n125\t    attention-score-driven, but the score-based mechanism remains the dominant driver\n126\t    (~40× stronger in median_diff). The weak recency signal at s030 reflects information-theoretic\n127\t    inevitability rather than the discrimination collapse mechanism.\n128\t\n129\t    '\n130\t  tables:\n131\t  - title: 'Table: Triple dissociation at s030'\n132\t    columns:\n133\t    - Strategy\n134\t    - median_diff\n135\t    - d_z\n136\t    - p_uncorrected\n137\t    - p_Bonferroni\n138\t    - Significant\n139\t    rows:\n140\t    - - Importance\n141\t      - '8.48'\n142\t      - '1.13'\n143\t      - <1e-79\n144\t      - <1e-79\n145\t      - 'Yes'\n146\t    - - Random\n147\t      - '0.51'\n148\t      - '0.35'\n149\t      - '0.006'\n150\t      - '0.018'\n151\t      - 'Yes'\n152\t    - - Recency\n153\t      - '0.21'\n154\t      - '0.32'\n155\t      - '0.028'\n156\t      - '0.084'\n157\t      - No (trend)\n158\t  - title: 'Table: Recency d_z dose-response across sparsities'\n159\t    columns:\n160\t    - Sparsity\n161\t    - d_z\n162\t    - p\n163\t    - Interpretation\n164\t    rows:\n165\t    - - s015\n166\t      - '0.083'\n167\t      - '0.77'\n168\t      - Null (negligible)\n169\t    - - s025\n170\t      - '0.14'\n171\t      - '0.38'\n172\t      - Null (negligible)\n173\t    - - s030\n174\t      - '0.32'\n175\t      - '0.028'\n176\t      - Weak (small, NS after Bonferroni)\n177\t  figures_description:\n178\t  - 'Line plot: d_z across sparsities for three strategies. Importance line rises\n179\t    steeply (0.57→0.95→1.13). Random line rises moderately (flat→0.15→0.35). Recency\n180\t    line stays near zero then upticks at s030 (0.08→0.14→0.32). Shaded region below\n181\t    d_z=0.2 marked as ''negligible''. Bonferroni significance threshold marked.'\n182\t  analysis: 's030 recency 弱信号是 median tier 的定义性特征。关键解读：(1) d_z=0.32 是 small effect，远低于\n183\t    importance 的 d_z=1.13（3.5× gap）；(2) Bonferroni 校正后 NS，统计 稳健性不足；(3) 机制与 importance\n184\t    不同——不是 discrimination collapse，而是 information loss 达到临界阈值后 phase-dependent context\n185\t    dependency 的自然反映。 Paper 叙事调整：C11 从 \"null at all sparsities\" 改为 \"null-to-weak,\n186\t    confirming primary mechanism is score-based\"。Discussion 新增 paragraph 解释 boundary\n187\t    condition。 Rebuttal 准备：即使 s030 recency 在 larger sample 中确认显著，effect size comparison\n188\t    (importance 40× stronger) 仍然支撑核心 claim。\n189\t\n190\t    '\n191\t- name: gpqa_ds_importance_s020\n192\t  plan_id: C10_gpqa_s020\n193\t  description: 'GPQA Diamond benchmark importance masking phase gradient at s=0.20,\n194\t    DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, n≈198. Extends GPQA cross-benchmark validation to\n195\t    second sparsity level.\n196\t\n197\t    '\n198\t  expected_results:\n199\t    n_problems: 198\n200\t    interaction_index:\n201\t      high:\n202\t        mean: 0.58\n203\t        median: 0.042\n204\t        ci:\n205\t        - 0.21\n206\t        - 1.15\n207\t        median_ci:\n208\t        - 0.035\n209\t        - 0.052\n210\t        winsorized_mean: 0.18\n211\t        skewness: 12.5\n212\t      mid:\n213\t        mean: 3.25\n214\t        median: 0.38\n215\t        ci:\n216\t        - 2.45\n217\t        - 4.21\n218\t        median_ci:\n219\t        - 0.32\n220\t        - 0.46\n221\t        winsorized_mean: 1.85\n222\t        skewness: 8.2\n223\t      low:\n224\t        mean: 18.4\n225\t        median: 2.85\n226\t        ci:\n227\t        - 15.2\n228\t        - 22.1\n229\t        median_ci:\n230\t        - 2.52\n231\t        - 3.25\n232\t        winsorized_mean: 12.3\n233\t        skewness: 7.6\n234\t    perplexity:\n235\t      high:\n236\t        dense: 1.178\n237\t        attn: 1.58\n238\t        kv: 1.92\n239\t        both: 2.85\n240\t      mid:\n241\t        dense: 1.308\n242\t        attn: 1.74\n243\t        kv: 4.85\n244\t        both: 8.12\n245\t      low:\n246\t        dense: 1.422\n247\t        attn: 2.15\n248\t        kv: 32.5\n249\t        both: 52.8\n250\t    phase_stats:\n251\t      high:\n252\t        n_tokens: 479658\n253\t        n_segments: 6261\n254\t      mid:\n255\t        n_tokens: 276409\n256\t        n_segments: 2185\n257\t      low:\n258\t        n_tokens: 465085\n259\t        n_segments: 5128\n260\t    pass_fail:\n261\t      ci_overlap: true\n262\t      sign_reversal: false\n263\t      overall: PASS\n264\t    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n265\t    median_ratio_low_high: 67.9\n266\t    median_difference: 2.81\n267\t    wilcoxon_p: <1e-35\n268\t    cohens_dz: 0.92\n269\t  result_rationale: 'GPQA s020 extends the dose-response curve established at s015.\n270\t    From MATH-500 reference, the s015→s020 scaling factor is approximately 3.8× (0.39→1.48).\n271\t    Applying a similar but slightly attenuated ratio to GPQA (given longer reasoning\n272\t    chains and harder problems that may show more gradual scaling): 0.95 × 3.0 ≈ 2.85.\n273\t    GPQA problems elicit longer reasoning chains than MATH-500 (~6000 tokens vs ~1200),\n274\t    meaning more tokens per problem and thus more stable per-problem statistics, but\n275\t    also more opportunity for compound interaction to accumulate. The gradient remains\n276\t    strongly monotonic (high < mid < low) with all phases well-separated. The effect\n277\t    size (d_z ≈ 0.92) places this solidly in the \"large\" range, consistent with the\n278\t    pattern that phase gradient is robust across benchmarks at the same sparsity level.\n279\t    The per-phase perplexity pattern shows KV-only degradation concentrating in low\n280\t    phase (dense ppl similar across phases, but kv/both ppl diverges dramatically),\n281\t    consistent with discrimination collapse preferentially affecting attention-heavy\n282\t    reasoning segments.\n283\t\n284\t    '\n285\t  tables:\n286\t  - title: 'Table: GPQA importance gradient dose-response (DS)'\n287\t    columns:\n288\t    - Sparsity\n289\t    - low_median\n290\t    - high_median\n291\t    - ratio\n292\t    - d_z\n293\t    - p\n294\t    rows:\n295\t    - - s015\n296\t      - '0.960'\n297\t      - '0.013'\n298\t      - 75.2×\n299\t      - '0.81'\n300\t      - <1e-29\n301\t    - - s020\n302\t      - '2.85'\n303\t      - '0.042'\n304\t      - 67.9×\n305\t      - '0.92'\n306\t      - <1e-35\n307\t  figures_description:\n308\t  - 'Dose-response bar chart: GPQA median_gradient (low-high) at s015 and s020. Clear\n309\t    monotonic increase. Inset comparison with MATH-500 same sparsities showing parallel\n310\t    trends but GPQA absolute values ~2.5× larger (due to longer chains).'\n311\t  analysis: 'GPQA s020 确认 phase gradient 在第三个 benchmark 上成立（MATH-500, GSM8K, GPQA）。\n312\t    Absolute magnitude 高于 MATH-500 同 sparsity (2.85 vs 1.48)，可能因为 GPQA 推理链 更长（更多 tokens\n313\t    累积 compound interaction）。关键：dose-response monotonicity 跨 benchmark 一致。Strategy\n314\t    specificity ratio 需要对应 GPQA random 实验才能计算； 基于 median tier 预测 ratio 在 2-3× 范围（类似\n315\t    GSM8K）。\n316\t\n317\t    '\n318\t- name: gpqa_ds_importance_s025\n319\t  plan_id: C10_gpqa_s025\n320\t  description: 'GPQA Diamond benchmark importance masking phase gradient at s=0.25,\n321\t    DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, n≈198. Third sparsity level for GPQA dose-response\n322\t    characterization.\n323\t\n324\t    '\n325\t  expected_results:\n326\t    n_problems: 198\n327\t    interaction_index:\n328\t      high:\n329\t        mean: 1.82\n330\t        median: 0.145\n331\t        ci:\n332\t        - 0.95\n333\t        - 3.12\n334\t        median_ci:\n335\t        - 0.115\n336\t        - 0.185\n337\t        winsorized_mean: 0.72\n338\t        skewness: 10.8\n339\t      mid:\n340\t        mean: 12.5\n341\t        median: 1.65\n342\t        ci:\n343\t        - 8.8\n344\t        - 17.2\n345\t        median_ci:\n346\t        - 1.35\n347\t        - 2.05\n348\t        winsorized_mean: 7.8\n349\t        skewness: 8.9\n350\t      low:\n351\t        mean: 52.3\n352\t        median: 8.2\n353\t        ci:\n354\t        - 40.5\n355\t        - 66.8\n356\t        median_ci:\n357\t        - 7.1\n358\t        - 9.5\n359\t        winsorized_mean: 35.6\n360\t        skewness: 7.2\n361\t    perplexity:\n362\t      high:\n363\t        dense: 1.178\n364\t        attn: 1.72\n365\t        kv: 2.35\n366\t        both: 4.15\n367\t      mid:\n368\t        dense: 1.308\n369\t        attn: 1.92\n370\t        kv: 8.5\n371\t        both: 18.6\n372\t      low:\n373\t        dense: 1.422\n374\t        attn: 2.45\n375\t        kv: 55.2\n376\t        both: 98.5\n377\t    phase_stats:\n378\t      high:\n379\t        n_tokens: 479658\n380\t        n_segments: 6261\n381\t      mid:\n382\t        n_tokens: 276409\n383\t        n_segments: 2185\n384\t      low:\n385\t        n_tokens: 465085\n386\t        n_segments: 5128\n387\t    pass_fail:\n388\t      ci_overlap: true\n389\t      sign_reversal: false\n390\t      overall: PASS\n391\t    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n392\t    median_ratio_low_high: 56.6\n393\t    median_difference: 8.06\n394\t    wilcoxon_p: <1e-42\n395\t    cohens_dz: 1.05\n396\t    gpqa_strategy_specificity_ratio_estimated: 2.5\n397\t  result_rationale: 'At s025, GPQA follows the same dose-response escalation pattern.\n398\t    From s020→s025 in MATH-500, the scaling factor is 4.8× (1.48→7.16). For GPQA,\n399\t    applying a modestly attenuated ratio (~2.8×) given the already-high baseline:\n400\t    2.85 × 2.8 ≈ 8.0. The attenuation reflects a ceiling effect as reasoning chains\n401\t    at GPQA difficulty level experience compound degradation more uniformly (the most\n402\t    complex reasoning steps are already heavily impacted at s020). The low/high ratio\n403\t    decreases slightly from 75× (s015) to 68× (s020) to 57× (s025) as high-phase II\n404\t    starts rising from its near-zero baseline. This mirrors MATH-500 where the ratio\n405\t    also peaks at lower sparsity. The d_z=1.05 (large) confirms that even at higher\n406\t    sparsity, the phase-dependent signal remains extremely robust on GPQA. For strategy\n407\t    specificity, based on the median tier and GSM8K precedent: GPQA imp/rand ratio\n408\t    is estimated at 2-3× (predicting ~2.5×), far below MATH-500''s 15-17× but consistent\n409\t    with the task-modulation narrative. Harder tasks with longer reasoning chains\n410\t    show weaker strategy specificity because even random eviction becomes increasingly\n411\t    damaging in a phase-dependent manner when chains are long.\n412\t\n413\t    '\n414\t  tables:\n415\t  - title: 'Table: GPQA full dose-response (importance, DS)'\n416\t    columns:\n417\t    - Sparsity\n418\t    - low_median\n419\t    - mid_median\n420\t    - high_median\n421\t    - gradient\n422\t    - d_z\n423\t    rows:\n424\t    - - s015\n425\t      - '0.960'\n426\t      - '0.102'\n427\t      - '0.013'\n428\t      - '0.947'\n429\t      - '0.81'\n430\t    - - s020\n431\t      - '2.85'\n432\t      - '0.38'\n433\t      - '0.042'\n434\t      - '2.81'\n435\t      - '0.92'\n436\t    - - s025\n437\t      - '8.20'\n438\t      - '1.65'\n439\t      - '0.145'\n440\t      - '8.06'\n441\t      - '1.05'\n442\t  - title: 'Table: Cross-benchmark strategy specificity ratio comparison'\n443\t    columns:\n444\t    - Benchmark\n445\t    - s025 imp/rand ratio\n446\t    - Task complexity\n447\t    rows:\n448\t    - - MATH-500\n449\t      - 15.5×\n450\t      - Medium (short chains)\n451\t    - - GSM8K\n452\t      - 3.8×\n453\t      - Low (very short chains)\n454\t    - - GPQA\n455\t      - ~2.5×\n456\t      - High (long chains)\n457\t  figures_description:\n458\t  - 'Three-panel dose-response figure: (A) GPQA phase gradient across s015-s025, monotonic\n459\t    with tightening CIs at higher n. (B) Cross-benchmark comparison of median_gradient\n460\t    at matched sparsities (MATH-500 vs GSM8K vs GPQA). (C) Strategy specificity ratio\n461\t    heatmap (benchmark × sparsity) showing clear task-dependence pattern.'\n462\t  analysis: 'GPQA s025 完成三点 dose-response，确认跨 benchmark monotonicity。关键发现： (1) Gradient\n463\t    magnitude 高于 MATH-500 (8.06 vs 7.16 at s025)——更长推理链累积更多 compound interaction；(2)\n464\t    Strategy specificity ratio (~2.5×) 继续 GSM8K 的衰减趋势， 进一步确认 task-modulation；(3) 低\n465\t    ratio 的机制解释：GPQA 推理链长(~6000 tokens)， 即使 random eviction 也在 longer chains 上产生 moderate\n466\t    phase gradient，压缩了 imp/rand gap。这为 reviewer 提供了清晰的 task-dependence 故事：chain length\n467\t    调制 strategy specificity 强度，而 phase gradient 本身跨 task 稳健。 C1 claim 最终形式：strategy\n468\t    specificity 是 task-modulated second-order finding， 不是 universal constant。\n469\t\n470\t    '\n471\t- name: gpqa_random_s025_predicted\n472\t  plan_id: C10_gpqa_rand\n473\t  description: 'Predicted GPQA random masking result needed to compute strategy specificity\n474\t    ratio. Not currently in registry but implied by median tier requiring imp/rand\n475\t    ratio calculation.\n476\t\n477\t    '\n478\t  expected_results:\n479\t    n_problems: 198\n480\t    low_phase_ii_median: 4.2\n481\t    high_phase_ii_median: 1.35\n482\t    median_gradient: 2.85\n483\t    median_gradient_ci:\n484\t    - 1.8\n485\t    - 4.1\n486\t    cohens_dz: 0.38\n487\t    wilcoxon_p: 0.0015\n488\t    imp_rand_ratio_s025: 2.83\n489\t  result_rationale: 'GPQA random masking at s025 is predicted to show a moderate phase\n490\t    gradient (d_z≈0.38, significant) because: (1) GPQA''s long reasoning chains mean\n491\t    even random token removal has phase-dependent impact (more accumulated context\n492\t    in low phase = more to lose); (2) this parallels GSM8K where random is significant\n493\t    at s025 (QW: d_z≈0.16 with ratio 3.8×); (3) GPQA''s longer chains amplify the\n494\t    random effect more than MATH-500. The resulting imp/rand ratio of ~2.8× fits squarely\n495\t    in the median tier''s predicted [1.8, 3.5] range and reinforces the narrative\n496\t    that strategy specificity is task-complexity-modulated.\n497\t\n498\t    '\n499\t  tables: []\n500\t  figures_description: []\n501\t  analysis: 'Strategy specificity ratio 在 GPQA 上的衰减 (2.8× vs MATH-500 的 15.5×) 是 median\n502\t    tier 的核心预测之一。机制：task complexity → chain length → random eviction 也产生 significant\n503\t    phase gradient → ratio 压缩。这不是 importance eviction 变弱 （GPQA importance gradient\n504\t    实际更强），而是 random eviction 在长链上变强。 Reviewer 可能质疑：如果 random 也显著，specificity claim\n505\t    是否成立？ Rebuttal：specificity 不是 binary (significant vs not)，而是 graded — importance\n506\t    consistently 2-3× stronger across all tested benchmarks，且在短链 benchmarks (MATH)\n507\t    上 specificity 极强 (15×)。\n508\t\n509\t    '\n510\t- name: c9_literature_differentiation\n511\t  plan_id: C9\n512\t  description: 'Non-experimental claim. Differentiation from Lethe/SparK/ThinKV/Physics-of-KV\n513\t    through Related Work positioning.\n514\t\n515\t    '\n516\t  expected_results:\n517\t    type: literature_review\n518\t    status: addressed_in_paper\n519\t    key_distinctions:\n520\t      vs_lethe: Method paper (adaptive eviction) vs empirical finding (phase-dependent\n521\t        severity)\n522\t      vs_spark: Treats compound interaction as uniform; we show it's phase×strategy\n523\t        modulated\n524\t      vs_thinkv: Single-axis phase-aware compression; we study dual-axis compound\n525\t        interaction\n526\t      vs_physics_kv: Single-axis compression-rate phase transition; we study reasoning-phase\n527\t        modulation\n528\t      vs_hies: Single-axis score collapse observation; we show compound amplification\n529\t        of collapse\n530\t      vs_rkv: Task-specific optimization method; we do mechanistic analysis\n531\t    citation_count_target: ≥50 (currently met)\n532\t  result_rationale: 'C9 不需要新实验——通过 Related Work §2 的结构化比较和 gap analysis 完成。Median\n533\t    tier 下 reviewer 可能仍认为 novelty 偏窄（\"incremental over existing phase-aware methods\"），\n534\t    reviewer_novelty_score 预期 2.8-3.3。应对：强调 experimental design contribution (recency\n535\t    as methodological control) 和 three-way interaction 的发现性质。\n536\t\n537\t    '\n538\t  tables: []\n539\t  figures_description: []\n540\t  analysis: 'Reviewer 对 novelty 的 median 评分 (2.8-3.3) 反映了一个现实：empirical finding paper\n541\t    在 novelty 维度天然弱于 method paper。应对策略：(1) 强调 no prior work 同时分析 compound × phase\n542\t    × strategy 三维交互；(2) C11 的 recency control 作为 experimental design novelty 是独特贡献（\"repurposing\n543\t    recency eviction as methodological control has no precedent\"）；(3) crossover phenomenon\n544\t    (C3) 是 全新发现，prior work 无法预测。\n545\t\n546\t    '\n547\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a5aac10-195d-47e9-909e-6fb532527f79","uuid":"4f51cdeb-04cc-4c11-9849-62f271c6381d","timestamp":"2026-05-17T01:24:22.025Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_11/projects/phase-gated-compound-sparse/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T005655/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '核心 claim（phase-modulated compound severity exists and is robust）不变，但\n  C11 从 ''scoring-independent eviction produces null gradient at all sparsities''\n  降级为 ''scoring-independent eviction produces null-to-weak gradient, confirming attention-score\n  mechanism is primary driver but not exclusive at extreme sparsity''。GPQA 跨 benchmark\n  扩展确认 phase gradient 普适性，但 strategy specificity ratio 继续衰减（2-3×），强化 task-modulation\n  叙事。Discussion 补充 boundary condition：extreme sparsity (s030) 下 任何 eviction 方法都可能触发弱\n  phase-dependent effects。Rebuttal 核心策略：effect size comparison（importance d_z >> recency\n  d_z 即使 s030 后者 nominally significant）。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: recency_s025\n  plan_id: C11_recency_s025\n  description: 'Recency-based eviction (scoring-independent control) at sparsity=0.25,\n    n=100, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B. Tests whether phase gradient remains null\n    at moderate-high sparsity.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 100\n    model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\n    masking_method: recency\n    sparsity: 0.25\n    phase_gradient_median_diff: 0.032\n    phase_gradient_median_diff_ci95:\n    - -0.08\n    - 0.16\n    cohens_dz: 0.14\n    p_value: 0.38\n    significant: false\n    low_phase_ii_median: 0.85\n    high_phase_ii_median: 0.78\n    low_high_ratio: 1.09\n    comparison_importance_s025_dz: 0.95\n    comparison_importance_s025_median_diff: 3.99\n    importance_vs_recency_ratio: ~125×\n    wilcoxon_p: 0.38\n    bonferroni_p_k3: 1.0\n  result_rationale: 'At s025, recency eviction removes the oldest 25% of KV entries\n    regardless of attention scores. Since discrimination collapse is driven by importance-score\n    judgment degradation after head pruning, recency eviction bypasses this mechanism\n    entirely. The slight positive trend (d_z=0.14) reflects marginal information loss\n    that differentially affects longer reasoning chains (low-sparsity phase has more\n    accumulated context to lose), but the effect is far below significance. The key\n    mechanistic argument holds: without attention-score-based selection, pruning doesn''t\n    create the biased pseudo-random degradation pattern that amplifies compound severity\n    in the low phase. At s025, total information loss from recency eviction is still\n    below the critical threshold where any removal method would trigger phase effects.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Triple dissociation at s025'\n    columns:\n    - Strategy\n    - median_diff\n    - d_z\n    - p\n    - Significant\n    rows:\n    - - Importance\n      - '3.99'\n      - '0.95'\n      - <1e-78\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Random\n      - '0.26'\n      - '0.15'\n      - 0.006 (Bonf.)\n      - Marginal\n    - - Recency\n      - '0.03'\n      - '0.14'\n      - '0.38'\n      - 'No'\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart showing phase gradient (median_diff) across three eviction strategies\n    at s025. Importance bar dominates (~4.0), random barely visible (~0.26), recency\n    near zero (~0.03). Error bars (95% CI) for recency cross zero.\n  analysis: 's025 结果与 s015 (d_z=0.083) 方向一致：recency 在 moderate sparsity 范围内不产生 显著\n    phase gradient。d_z 从 0.083 升至 0.14 表明存在微弱的 sparsity-dependent 趋势， 但仍远低于 importance\n    的 d_z=0.95。Triple dissociation 在 s025 水平进一步确认： phase gradient 是 attention-score\n    mechanism 的特有产物。Random 在 s025 的 marginal significance (n=500 数据 Bonf. p=0.006)\n    与 recency NS 的对比值得注意——random masking 虽然不使用 importance scores，但其均匀采样仍受 head pruning\n    后 score distribution 变化的间接影响；recency 完全脱离 score pathway，因此更 clean 作为 control。\n\n    '\n- name: recency_s030\n  plan_id: C11_recency_s030\n  description: 'Recency-based eviction at sparsity=0.30 (extreme), n=100. Tests whether\n    extreme information loss triggers weak phase-dependent effects even without score-based\n    selection.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 100\n    model: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B\n    masking_method: recency\n    sparsity: 0.3\n    phase_gradient_median_diff: 0.21\n    phase_gradient_median_diff_ci95:\n    - 0.02\n    - 0.45\n    cohens_dz: 0.32\n    p_value: 0.028\n    significant_uncorrected: true\n    significant_bonferroni_k3: false\n    bonferroni_p: 0.084\n    low_phase_ii_median: 1.95\n    high_phase_ii_median: 1.62\n    low_high_ratio: 1.2\n    comparison_importance_s030_dz: 1.13\n    comparison_importance_s030_median_diff: 8.48\n    importance_vs_recency_dz_ratio: 3.5×\n    importance_vs_recency_mediandiff_ratio: ~40×\n    wilcoxon_p: 0.028\n  result_rationale: 'At extreme sparsity (s030), 30% of attention heads are pruned\n    AND the oldest 30% of KV cache is evicted. Even though recency eviction doesn''t\n    use attention scores, the sheer volume of information loss reaches a critical\n    threshold where phase-dependent effects emerge through a different mechanism:\n    low-sparsity phase (reasoning-heavy) relies more heavily on accumulated context\n    from earlier tokens, and recency eviction disproportionately removes this early\n    context. The effect is genuine but weak (d_z=0.32 vs importance d_z=1.13) and\n    fails Bonferroni correction (k=3 strategies tested at s030). This establishes\n    the boundary condition: at extreme sparsity, phase-dependent severity is not exclusively\n    attention-score-driven, but the score-based mechanism remains the dominant driver\n    (~40× stronger in median_diff). The weak recency signal at s030 reflects information-theoretic\n    inevitability rather than the discrimination collapse mechanism.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: Triple dissociation at s030'\n    columns:\n    - Strategy\n    - median_diff\n    - d_z\n    - p_uncorrected\n    - p_Bonferroni\n    - Significant\n    rows:\n    - - Importance\n      - '8.48'\n      - '1.13'\n      - <1e-79\n      - <1e-79\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Random\n      - '0.51'\n      - '0.35'\n      - '0.006'\n      - '0.018'\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - Recency\n      - '0.21'\n      - '0.32'\n      - '0.028'\n      - '0.084'\n      - No (trend)\n  - title: 'Table: Recency d_z dose-response across sparsities'\n    columns:\n    - Sparsity\n    - d_z\n    - p\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - s015\n      - '0.083'\n      - '0.77'\n      - Null (negligible)\n    - - s025\n      - '0.14'\n      - '0.38'\n      - Null (negligible)\n    - - s030\n      - '0.32'\n      - '0.028'\n      - Weak (small, NS after Bonferroni)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: d_z across sparsities for three strategies. Importance line rises\n    steeply (0.57→0.95→1.13). Random line rises moderately (flat→0.15→0.35). Recency\n    line stays near zero then upticks at s030 (0.08→0.14→0.32). Shaded region below\n    d_z=0.2 marked as ''negligible''. Bonferroni significance threshold marked.'\n  analysis: 's030 recency 弱信号是 median tier 的定义性特征。关键解读：(1) d_z=0.32 是 small effect，远低于\n    importance 的 d_z=1.13（3.5× gap）；(2) Bonferroni 校正后 NS，统计 稳健性不足；(3) 机制与 importance\n    不同——不是 discrimination collapse，而是 information loss 达到临界阈值后 phase-dependent context\n    dependency 的自然反映。 Paper 叙事调整：C11 从 \"null at all sparsities\" 改为 \"null-to-weak,\n    confirming primary mechanism is score-based\"。Discussion 新增 paragraph 解释 boundary\n    condition。 Rebuttal 准备：即使 s030 recency 在 larger sample 中确认显著，effect size comparison\n    (importance 40× stronger) 仍然支撑核心 claim。\n\n    '\n- name: gpqa_ds_importance_s020\n  plan_id: C10_gpqa_s020\n  description: 'GPQA Diamond benchmark importance masking phase gradient at s=0.20,\n    DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, n≈198. Extends GPQA cross-benchmark validation to\n    second sparsity level.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 198\n    interaction_index:\n      high:\n        mean: 0.58\n        median: 0.042\n        ci:\n        - 0.21\n        - 1.15\n        median_ci:\n        - 0.035\n        - 0.052\n        winsorized_mean: 0.18\n        skewness: 12.5\n      mid:\n        mean: 3.25\n        median: 0.38\n        ci:\n        - 2.45\n        - 4.21\n        median_ci:\n        - 0.32\n        - 0.46\n        winsorized_mean: 1.85\n        skewness: 8.2\n      low:\n        mean: 18.4\n        median: 2.85\n        ci:\n        - 15.2\n        - 22.1\n        median_ci:\n        - 2.52\n        - 3.25\n        winsorized_mean: 12.3\n        skewness: 7.6\n    perplexity:\n      high:\n        dense: 1.178\n        attn: 1.58\n        kv: 1.92\n        both: 2.85\n      mid:\n        dense: 1.308\n        attn: 1.74\n        kv: 4.85\n        both: 8.12\n      low:\n        dense: 1.422\n        attn: 2.15\n        kv: 32.5\n        both: 52.8\n    phase_stats:\n      high:\n        n_tokens: 479658\n        n_segments: 6261\n      mid:\n        n_tokens: 276409\n        n_segments: 2185\n      low:\n        n_tokens: 465085\n        n_segments: 5128\n    pass_fail:\n      ci_overlap: true\n      sign_reversal: false\n      overall: PASS\n    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n    median_ratio_low_high: 67.9\n    median_difference: 2.81\n    wilcoxon_p: <1e-35\n    cohens_dz: 0.92\n  result_rationale: 'GPQA s020 extends the dose-response curve established at s015.\n    From MATH-500 reference, the s015→s020 scaling factor is approximately 3.8× (0.39→1.48).\n    Applying a similar but slightly attenuated ratio to GPQA (given longer reasoning\n    chains and harder problems that may show more gradual scaling): 0.95 × 3.0 ≈ 2.85.\n    GPQA problems elicit longer reasoning chains than MATH-500 (~6000 tokens vs ~1200),\n    meaning more tokens per problem and thus more stable per-problem statistics, but\n    also more opportunity for compound interaction to accumulate. The gradient remains\n    strongly monotonic (high < mid < low) with all phases well-separated. The effect\n    size (d_z ≈ 0.92) places this solidly in the \"large\" range, consistent with the\n    pattern that phase gradient is robust across benchmarks at the same sparsity level.\n    The per-phase perplexity pattern shows KV-only degradation concentrating in low\n    phase (dense ppl similar across phases, but kv/both ppl diverges dramatically),\n    consistent with discrimination collapse preferentially affecting attention-heavy\n    reasoning segments.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: GPQA importance gradient dose-response (DS)'\n    columns:\n    - Sparsity\n    - low_median\n    - high_median\n    - ratio\n    - d_z\n    - p\n    rows:\n    - - s015\n      - '0.960'\n      - '0.013'\n      - 75.2×\n      - '0.81'\n      - <1e-29\n    - - s020\n      - '2.85'\n      - '0.042'\n      - 67.9×\n      - '0.92'\n      - <1e-35\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dose-response bar chart: GPQA median_gradient (low-high) at s015 and s020. Clear\n    monotonic increase. Inset comparison with MATH-500 same sparsities showing parallel\n    trends but GPQA absolute values ~2.5× larger (due to longer chains).'\n  analysis: 'GPQA s020 确认 phase gradient 在第三个 benchmark 上成立（MATH-500, GSM8K, GPQA）。\n    Absolute magnitude 高于 MATH-500 同 sparsity (2.85 vs 1.48)，可能因为 GPQA 推理链 更长（更多 tokens\n    累积 compound interaction）。关键：dose-response monotonicity 跨 benchmark 一致。Strategy\n    specificity ratio 需要对应 GPQA random 实验才能计算； 基于 median tier 预测 ratio 在 2-3× 范围（类似\n    GSM8K）。\n\n    '\n- name: gpqa_ds_importance_s025\n  plan_id: C10_gpqa_s025\n  description: 'GPQA Diamond benchmark importance masking phase gradient at s=0.25,\n    DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, n≈198. Third sparsity level for GPQA dose-response\n    characterization.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 198\n    interaction_index:\n      high:\n        mean: 1.82\n        median: 0.145\n        ci:\n        - 0.95\n        - 3.12\n        median_ci:\n        - 0.115\n        - 0.185\n        winsorized_mean: 0.72\n        skewness: 10.8\n      mid:\n        mean: 12.5\n        median: 1.65\n        ci:\n        - 8.8\n        - 17.2\n        median_ci:\n        - 1.35\n        - 2.05\n        winsorized_mean: 7.8\n        skewness: 8.9\n      low:\n        mean: 52.3\n        median: 8.2\n        ci:\n        - 40.5\n        - 66.8\n        median_ci:\n        - 7.1\n        - 9.5\n        winsorized_mean: 35.6\n        skewness: 7.2\n    perplexity:\n      high:\n        dense: 1.178\n        attn: 1.72\n        kv: 2.35\n        both: 4.15\n      mid:\n        dense: 1.308\n        attn: 1.92\n        kv: 8.5\n        both: 18.6\n      low:\n        dense: 1.422\n        attn: 2.45\n        kv: 55.2\n        both: 98.5\n    phase_stats:\n      high:\n        n_tokens: 479658\n        n_segments: 6261\n      mid:\n        n_tokens: 276409\n        n_segments: 2185\n      low:\n        n_tokens: 465085\n        n_segments: 5128\n    pass_fail:\n      ci_overlap: true\n      sign_reversal: false\n      overall: PASS\n    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n    median_ratio_low_high: 56.6\n    median_difference: 8.06\n    wilcoxon_p: <1e-42\n    cohens_dz: 1.05\n    gpqa_strategy_specificity_ratio_estimated: 2.5\n  result_rationale: 'At s025, GPQA follows the same dose-response escalation pattern.\n    From s020→s025 in MATH-500, the scaling factor is 4.8× (1.48→7.16). For GPQA,\n    applying a modestly attenuated ratio (~2.8×) given the already-high baseline:\n    2.85 × 2.8 ≈ 8.0. The attenuation reflects a ceiling effect as reasoning chains\n    at GPQA difficulty level experience compound degradation more uniformly (the most\n    complex reasoning steps are already heavily impacted at s020). The low/high ratio\n    decreases slightly from 75× (s015) to 68× (s020) to 57× (s025) as high-phase II\n    starts rising from its near-zero baseline. This mirrors MATH-500 where the ratio\n    also peaks at lower sparsity. The d_z=1.05 (large) confirms that even at higher\n    sparsity, the phase-dependent signal remains extremely robust on GPQA. For strategy\n    specificity, based on the median tier and GSM8K precedent: GPQA imp/rand ratio\n    is estimated at 2-3× (predicting ~2.5×), far below MATH-500''s 15-17× but consistent\n    with the task-modulation narrative. Harder tasks with longer reasoning chains\n    show weaker strategy specificity because even random eviction becomes increasingly\n    damaging in a phase-dependent manner when chains are long.\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table: GPQA full dose-response (importance, DS)'\n    columns:\n    - Sparsity\n    - low_median\n    - mid_median\n    - high_median\n    - gradient\n    - d_z\n    rows:\n    - - s015\n      - '0.960'\n      - '0.102'\n      - '0.013'\n      - '0.947'\n      - '0.81'\n    - - s020\n      - '2.85'\n      - '0.38'\n      - '0.042'\n      - '2.81'\n      - '0.92'\n    - - s025\n      - '8.20'\n      - '1.65'\n      - '0.145'\n      - '8.06'\n      - '1.05'\n  - title: 'Table: Cross-benchmark strategy specificity ratio comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - s025 imp/rand ratio\n    - Task complexity\n    rows:\n    - - MATH-500\n      - 15.5×\n      - Medium (short chains)\n    - - GSM8K\n      - 3.8×\n      - Low (very short chains)\n    - - GPQA\n      - ~2.5×\n      - High (long chains)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Three-panel dose-response figure: (A) GPQA phase gradient across s015-s025, monotonic\n    with tightening CIs at higher n. (B) Cross-benchmark comparison of median_gradient\n    at matched sparsities (MATH-500 vs GSM8K vs GPQA). (C) Strategy specificity ratio\n    heatmap (benchmark × sparsity) showing clear task-dependence pattern.'\n  analysis: 'GPQA s025 完成三点 dose-response，确认跨 benchmark monotonicity。关键发现： (1) Gradient\n    magnitude 高于 MATH-500 (8.06 vs 7.16 at s025)——更长推理链累积更多 compound interaction；(2)\n    Strategy specificity ratio (~2.5×) 继续 GSM8K 的衰减趋势， 进一步确认 task-modulation；(3) 低\n    ratio 的机制解释：GPQA 推理链长(~6000 tokens)， 即使 random eviction 也在 longer chains 上产生 moderate\n    phase gradient，压缩了 imp/rand gap。这为 reviewer 提供了清晰的 task-dependence 故事：chain length\n    调制 strategy specificity 强度，而 phase gradient 本身跨 task 稳健。 C1 claim 最终形式：strategy\n    specificity 是 task-modulated second-order finding， 不是 universal constant。\n\n    '\n- name: gpqa_random_s025_predicted\n  plan_id: C10_gpqa_rand\n  description: 'Predicted GPQA random masking result needed to compute strategy specificity\n    ratio. Not currently in registry but implied by median tier requiring imp/rand\n    ratio calculation.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 198\n    low_phase_ii_median: 4.2\n    high_phase_ii_median: 1.35\n    median_gradient: 2.85\n    median_gradient_ci:\n    - 1.8\n    - 4.1\n    cohens_dz: 0.38\n    wilcoxon_p: 0.0015\n    imp_rand_ratio_s025: 2.83\n  result_rationale: 'GPQA random masking at s025 is predicted to show a moderate phase\n    gradient (d_z≈0.38, significant) because: (1) GPQA''s long reasoning chains mean\n    even random token removal has phase-dependent impact (more accumulated context\n    in low phase = more to lose); (2) this parallels GSM8K where random is significant\n    at s025 (QW: d_z≈0.16 with ratio 3.8×); (3) GPQA''s longer chains amplify the\n    random effect more than MATH-500. The resulting imp/rand ratio of ~2.8× fits squarely\n    in the median tier''s predicted [1.8, 3.5] range and reinforces the narrative\n    that strategy specificity is task-complexity-modulated.\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Strategy specificity ratio 在 GPQA 上的衰减 (2.8× vs MATH-500 的 15.5×) 是 median\n    tier 的核心预测之一。机制：task complexity → chain length → random eviction 也产生 significant\n    phase gradient → ratio 压缩。这不是 importance eviction 变弱 （GPQA importance gradient\n    实际更强），而是 random eviction 在长链上变强。 Reviewer 可能质疑：如果 random 也显著，specificity claim\n    是否成立？ Rebuttal：specificity 不是 binary (significant vs not)，而是 graded — importance\n    consistently 2-3× stronger across all tested benchmarks，且在短链 benchmarks (MATH)\n    上 specificity 极强 (15×)。\n\n    '\n- name: c9_literature_differentiation\n  plan_id: C9\n  description: 'Non-experimental claim. Differentiation from Lethe/SparK/ThinKV/Physics-of-KV\n    through Related Work positioning.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    type: literature_review\n    status: addressed_in_paper\n    key_distinctions:\n      vs_lethe: Method paper (adaptive eviction) vs empirical finding (phase-dependent\n        severity)\n      vs_spark: Treats compound interaction as uniform; we show it's phase×strategy\n        modulated\n      vs_thinkv: Single-axis phase-aware compression; we study dual-axis compound\n        interaction\n      vs_physics_kv: Single-axis compression-rate phase transition; we study reasoning-phase\n        modulation\n      vs_hies: Single-axis score collapse observation; we show compound amplification\n        of collapse\n      vs_rkv: Task-specific optimization method; we do mechanistic analysis\n    citation_count_target: ≥50 (currently met)\n  result_rationale: 'C9 不需要新实验——通过 Related Work §2 的结构化比较和 gap analysis 完成。Median\n    tier 下 reviewer 可能仍认为 novelty 偏窄（\"incremental over existing phase-aware methods\"），\n    reviewer_novelty_score 预期 2.8-3.3。应对：强调 experimental design contribution (recency\n    as methodological control) 和 three-way interaction 的发现性质。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Reviewer 对 novelty 的 median 评分 (2.8-3.3) 反映了一个现实：empirical finding paper\n    在 novelty 维度天然弱于 method paper。应对策略：(1) 强调 no prior work 同时分析 compound × phase\n    × strategy 三维交互；(2) C11 的 recency control 作为 experimental design novelty 是独特贡献（\"repurposing\n    recency eviction as methodological control has no precedent\"）；(3) crossover phenomenon\n    (C3) 是 全新发现，prior work 无法预测。\n\n    '\n","numLines":547,"startLine":1,"totalLines":547}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Wiy8K8hNDqmmiz7X1rbLnX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've read the full PDF paper and the review context YAML. Now I need to dispatch two reviewers for a full roundtable review process:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nLet me launch both reviewers in parallel, then conduct the roundtable process.\n\nLet me carefully analyze the paper first to understand what I'm working with:\n\n**Paper Summary**: \"Phase-Gated Compound Sparsity\" argues that when attention head pruning and KV cache eviction are applied jointly (compound sparsity), the resulting degradation is not uniform but varies systematically across reasoning phases. Importance-based eviction produces strong phase-dependent gradients, while recency-based (scoring-independent) eviction produces null-to-weak gradients, confirming the attention-score mechanism as primary driver.\n\n\nNow I'm looking at the core experimental setup: recency-based eviction controls across multiple sparsity levels on MATH-500, cross-benchmark validation on GPQA Diamond, and how the strategy specificity ratio behaves across different datasets. The review context flags that the C11 claim was refined from claiming null effects uniformly to null-to-weak effects, and the specificity ratio continues showing 2-3× decay with extended phase coverage.\n\nI need to examine gradient universality properties and what happens at the extreme sparsity boundary before moving forward with the reviewer dispatch.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24415,"cache_read_input_tokens":24215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24415},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":nul